// THE GHOST GUARDS STAND AT THEIR GATES, which they were not doing.
//
// Four of them, two to a barrier, and the config declared no wanderrange - so they took the
// engine's default of five and drifted. Measured: a north-gate guard spawned at 3658,3508 was
// found five tiles west at 3653,3508, which is past the corner of the wall it is supposed to be
// guarding.
//
// That is cosmetic on its own and not cosmetic once they take a toll. phasmatys_townsfolk.rs2 pays
// the toll and then hands the player to ~ahoy_step_through, the barrier's own crossing code, which
// moves them two tiles across the wall FROM WHERE THEY ARE STANDING - and p_teleport does not check
// collision. A guard five tiles off its post means a player standing next to that guard, nowhere
// near the gate, being stepped two tiles into whatever is there. Pinning the guards is what makes
// the toll safe to take, so this file and that script go together.
//
// Same field and same reason as wom_bed_inactive's wanderrange=0 in all.npc, and the same reason
// king_bolren stands still where he answered the bell.
//
// Moved out of _unpack/377/all.npc rather than edited in place, because redeclaring a config is a
// duplicate-config error - the convention area_lostcity/configs/zanaris_gate.loc set. Everything
// below is the cache's own, byte for byte, with one line added.

[ahoy_ghost_guard]
name=Ghost Guard
desc=This ghost guards the gates of Port Phasmatys.
model1=npc_1686
model2=npc_1684i2
model3=npc_1684i3
model4=npc_1684i4
recol1s=14861
recol1d=15950
walkanim=human_walk_f,human_walk_b,human_walk_l,human_walk_r
readyanim=human_ready
resizev=112
resizeh=112
ambient=35
contrast=35
op1=Talk-To
vislevel=hide
head1=npc_1686_head
wanderrange=0
